---ContainerPort represents a network port in a single container.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerPort
---@field containerPort number containerPort is the number of port to expose on the pod's IP address. This must be a valid port number, 0 < x < 65536.
---@field hostIP? string hostIP is the host IP to bind the external port to.
---@field hostPort? number hostPort is the number of port to expose on the host. If specified, this must be a valid port number, 0 < x < 65536. If HostNetwork is specified, this must match ContainerPort. Most containers do not need this.
---@field name? string name is the name of the port. If specified, this must be an IANA_SVC_NAME and unique within the pod. Each named port in a pod must have a unique name. Name for the port that can be referred to by services.
---@field protocol? string protocol is the protocol for port. Must be UDP, TCP, or SCTP. Defaults to "TCP".

---ports is the list of ports to expose from the container. Not specifying a port here DOES NOT prevent that port from being exposed. Any port which is listening on the default "0.0.0.0" address inside a container will be accessible from the network. Modifying this array with strategic merge patch may corrupt the data. For more information See https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/108255. Cannot be updated.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerPortsList kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerPort[]

---ContainerResizePolicy represents resource resize policy for the container.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerResizePolicy
---@field resourceName string resourceName is the name of the resource to which this resource resize policy applies. Supported values: cpu, memory.
---@field restartPolicy string restartPolicy is the restart policy to apply when specified resource is resized. If not specified, it defaults to NotRequired.

---resizePolicy is the resize policy for the container. This field cannot be set on ephemeral containers.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerResizePolicyList kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerResizePolicy[]

---restartPolicyRules represents a list of rules to be checked to determine if the container should be restarted on exit. The rules are evaluated in order. Once a rule matches a container exit condition, the remaining rules are ignored. If no rule matches the container exit condition, the Container-level restart policy determines the whether the container is restarted or not. Constraints on the rules: - At most 20 rules are allowed. - Rules can have the same action. - Identical rules are not forbidden in validations. When rules are specified, container MUST set RestartPolicy explicitly even it if matches the Pod's RestartPolicy.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartPolicyRulesList kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRule[]

---ContainerRestartRule describes how a container exit is handled.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRule
---@field action string action specifies the action taken on a container exit if the requirements are satisfied. The only possible value is "Restart" to restart the container.
---@field exitCodes? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRuleOnExitCodes exitCodes represents the exit codes to check on container exits.

---ContainerRestartRuleOnExitCodes describes the condition for handling an exited container based on its exit codes.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRuleOnExitCodes
---@field operator string operator represents the relationship between the container exit code(s) and the specified values. Possible values are: - In: the requirement is satisfied if the container exit code is in the set of specified values. - NotIn: the requirement is satisfied if the container exit code is not in the set of specified values.
---@field values? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRuleOnExitCodesValuesList values specifies the set of values to check for container exit codes. At most 255 elements are allowed.

---values specifies the set of values to check for container exit codes. At most 255 elements are allowed.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ContainerRestartRuleOnExitCodesValuesList number[]

