---ResourceRequirements describes the compute resource requirements.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceRequirements
---@field claims? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceRequirementsClaimsList claims lists the names of resources, defined in spec.resourceClaims, that are used by this container. This field is immutable. It can only be set for containers.
---@field limits? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceRequirementsLimitsMap limits describes the maximum amount of compute resources allowed. For kubelet cgroup enforcement: - cpu and memory: a limit of 0 is treated the same as an unspecified limit. If neither the container nor the pod specifies a limit, the resource is not limited. - hugepages: an unspecified limit is treated the same as a limit of 0. More details: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/
---@field requests? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceRequirementsRequestsMap requests describes the minimum amount of compute resources required. If Requests is omitted for a container, it defaults to Limits if that is explicitly specified, otherwise to an implementation-defined value. Requests cannot exceed Limits. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/

---claims lists the names of resources, defined in spec.resourceClaims, that are used by this container.
---
---This field is immutable. It can only be set for containers.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceRequirementsClaimsList kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1ResourceClaim[]

