---Adapts a secret into a projected volume.
---
---The contents of the target Secret's Data field will be presented in a projected volume as files using the keys in the Data field as the file names. Note that this is identical to a secret volume source without the default mode.
---@class kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1SecretProjection
---@field items? kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1SecretProjectionItemsList items if unspecified, each key-value pair in the Data field of the referenced Secret will be projected into the volume as a file whose name is the key and content is the value. If specified, the listed keys will be projected into the specified paths, and unlisted keys will not be present. If a key is specified which is not present in the Secret, the volume setup will error unless it is marked optional. Paths must be relative and may not contain the '..' path or start with '..'.
---@field name? string name of the referent. This field is effectively required, but due to backwards compatibility is allowed to be empty. Instances of this type with an empty value here are almost certainly wrong. More info: https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/overview/working-with-objects/names/#names
---@field optional? boolean optional field specify whether the Secret or its key must be defined

---items if unspecified, each key-value pair in the Data field of the referenced Secret will be projected into the volume as a file whose name is the key and content is the value. If specified, the listed keys will be projected into the specified paths, and unlisted keys will not be present. If a key is specified which is not present in the Secret, the volume setup will error unless it is marked optional. Paths must be relative and may not contain the '..' path or start with '..'.
---@alias kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1SecretProjectionItemsList kubernetes.core.IoK8sApiCoreV1KeyToPath[]

---SecretReference represents a Secret Reference. It has enough information to retrieve secret in any namespace
